ecystitis: Less likely due to absence of jaundice or elevated liver enzymes (not yet confirmed)", "Acute Pancreatitis: Typically presents with periumbilical or epigastric pain, not localized right upper quadrant", "Acute Appendicitis: Usually presents with periumbilical to right lower quadrant migration, not right upper quadrant", "Anorexia Nervosa-Related Complication: Constitutional symptoms present but overshadowed by acute haemodynamic instability"], "alarm_features": ["Hypotension with tachycardia (shock)", "Severe localized right upper quadrant pain", "Sexual activity without contraception", "Recent significant weight loss"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Gynecologic / Pelvic Emergency", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.4832214765100671, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Absence of jaundice weakens the case for acute biliary obstruction (B3) but does not exclude it entirely, as atypical presentations can occur."], "evidence_against": ["Right upper quadrant pain is more specific to biliary/hepatic pathology (B2/B3) than gynecologic causes, but absence of vaginal bleeding weakens B1."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Hepatic / Hepatobiliary Vascular Emergency", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.25, "posterior": 0.3020134228187919, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Right upper quadrant pain is more characteristic of biliary pathology (B2/B3) than pancreatic emergencies (B4), which typically present epigastrically."], "evidence_against": ["Acute pain exacerbation during exercise 